mbers: append ticket/subticket members to a PENDING run (duplicates rejected, positions continue after existing members).", "properties": {"homeId": {"description": "Stable public identifier of one OMT home. Every public reference in the protocol must be qualified with a HomeId (R4). Bare filesystem/workspace paths are DSH-adapter compatibility inputs and are resolved to a HomeId before anything crosses the wire.", "pattern": "^h_[a-z0-9]{6,}$", "type": "string"}, "nodeIds": {"items": {"description": "Ticket node identifier within one home, e.g. TICKET-0001, EPIC-0003.", "pattern": "^[A-Z][A-Z0-9]*-[0-9]+$", "type": "string"}, "minItems": 1, "type": "array"}, "runId": {"description": "Run identifier within one home, e.g. RUN-0001.", "pattern": "^RUN-[0-9]+$", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["homeId", "runId", "nodeIds"], "type": "object"}}, {"name": "mcp__omt__run__nudge_record", "description": "Method run/nudge-record: record a continuation nudge; nodeId targets one pending item, omission nudges every pending item of the run.", "parameters": {"description": "Method run/nudge-record: record a continuation nudge; nodeId targets one pending item, omission nudges every pending item of the run.", "properties": {"homeId": {"description": "Stable public identifier of one OMT home. Every public reference in the protocol must be qualified with a HomeId (R4). Bare filesystem/workspace paths are DSH-adapter compatibility inputs and are resolved to a HomeId before anything crosses the wire.", "pattern": "^h_[a-z0-9]{6,}$", "type": "string"}, "nodeId": {"description": "Ticket node identifier within one home, e.g. TICKET-0001, EPIC-0003.", "pattern": "^[A-Z][A-Z0-9]*-[0-9]+$", "type": "string"}, "runId": {"description": "Run identifier within one home, e.g. RUN-0001.", "pattern": "^RUN-[0-9]+$", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["homeId", "runId"], "type": "object"}}, {"name": "mcp__omt__run__interrupt", "description": "Method run/interrupt: demote every in-flight item of a runn